1
00:00:00,402 --> 00:00:02,402
(Sheldon:)So, what are we making today?

2
00:00:02,571 --> 00:00:06,781
(Howard:)A small payload support structure for
a European science experimental package...

3
00:00:06,951 --> 00:00:10,491
(Howard:)- ...that's going up on the next space shuttle.
- Really? How does it work?

4
00:00:10,663 --> 00:00:12,793
(Howard:)It will be attached to the payload bay...

5
00:00:12,957 --> 00:00:16,547
(Howard:)...and the sensor apparatus will rest on it.

6
00:00:16,961 --> 00:00:18,171
Aha.

7
00:00:18,629 --> 00:00:21,129
(Sheldon:)So it's a shelf.

8
00:00:24,134 --> 00:00:25,304
(Howard:)No, you don't understand.

9
00:00:25,469 --> 00:00:28,759
(Howard:)During acceleration, it needs
to stay perfectly level and provide...

10
00:00:28,931 --> 00:00:30,351
(Howard:)Yeah, okay, it's a shelf.

11
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:32,640
(Sheldon:)I notice you're using titanium.

12
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:35,140
(Sheldon:)Did you give any consideration
to carbon nanotubes?

13
00:00:35,312 --> 00:00:38,272
(Sheldon:)They're lighter, cheaper
and have twice the tensile strength.

14
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:44,030
(Howard:)Sheldon, there's a diploma in my office
that says I have a master's in engineering.

15
00:00:44,196 --> 00:00:48,036
(Sheldon:)And you also have a note from your mother
that says, "I love you, Bubula."

16
00:00:49,868 --> 00:00:53,708
(Sheldon:)But neither of those is a cogent argument
for titanium over nanotubes.

17
00:00:54,456 --> 00:00:55,706
(Sheldon:)- Sheldon.
- Yes?

18
00:00:55,874 --> 00:00:58,044
(Leonard:)Go away.

19
00:00:58,669 --> 00:01:00,209
(Sheldon:)Did Leonard tell you to say that?

